# Core architecture — always applies

Full reasoning lives in `docs/decisions/` (DR-001, DR-002, …). Index: `docs/README.md`.
When a decision isn't covered by these rules, read those files; if still unclear, ASK — do not
invent a decision.

## Framework reality (this repo specifically)
This Next.js version has breaking changes vs. training data (see `AGENTS.md`). Before writing
ANY Next.js or Prisma API, verify the current API in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`. Never write
these APIs from memory. State what the local docs say, then write the code.

## Module boundaries
- Business logic lives in `src/modules/<feature>/`, never in `app/`.
- `app/` is routes only: Server Actions do validate → authorize → delegate. No business logic.
- Three layers per module: `domain/` (pure functions, no DB, no await), `application/` (use
  cases, await + transactions), `infrastructure/` (all Prisma queries).
- Dependencies point DOWN only. `payment/` never imports `booking/`. Never an upward import.
- One slice at a time. Do not scaffold folders/files ahead of the current task.

## Hard integrity rules (never violate)
- `tenant_id` on EVERY tenant-owned table, including child tables. No exceptions.
- Money is always `Decimal`, never a JS float. USD `Decimal(12,2)`, LBP `Decimal(18,0)`.
- Ledger row + its cause (payment/expense) are written in the SAME `$transaction`. Always.
- Notifications happen AFTER the transaction commits, never inside it.
- Payment links to source by `source_type + source_id` (polymorphic). No `booking_id` on payments.
- Tenant context comes from the URL (subdomain → header). Session only authorizes against it.
- Domain functions take interfaces (e.g. `BookingLike`), not concrete Prisma types.

## Testing (Jest)
- Jest is the project test runner. Ship tests with each slice for `domain/` and other pure
  helpers; follow `docs/guides/testing-jest.md`. SPECs list expected coverage under **Tests**.

## Style
- Functions, not classes, unless there's a real reason.
- Keep responses scoped to the current task. Don't refactor unrelated code.
- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones.
- After a finished SPEC step or notable decision, append to `docs/progress.md`
  (see `.cursor/rules/050-progress-log.mdc`). Do not rewrite that log.
